# Templates

:lead Rocci templates provide HTML templating for Roc applications. The core functionality is pure templates, with no assumptions on the rest of the stack. See [Applications](/docs/applications) for full standalone Rocci application development.

Rocci templates are inspired by golang [templ](https://templ.guide) templating language, which integrate HTML tags into normal Go code functions, which is then generated as pure Go code by the generator.


:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/components/", title: "Components", summary: "Declare, call, preview, and fixtures."]
    :link-card[href: "/docs/templates/markup/", title: "Markup", summary: "Tags, attributes, interpolations, scoped CSS, stable ids."]
